<http://data.silknow.org/object/57094db5-6b58-3018-9abe-2f9bf8bfc4ff/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Description: silk satin brocaded with silk and metal thread,\nDark blue ground with a pattern of confronting birds above a circular arrangement of three flowers on a stem with a pair of leaves at the bottom.  In between this arrangement is a small floral sprig and above the arrangement is a small flame-like tree. The birds were woven with either light blue or green [visible now only from the back] details.  The predominate colours are pink and white.  The metal thread is silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk.\n\nSee also T.210-1910 for the same design on a smaller scale."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/57094db5-6b58-3018-9abe-2f9bf8bfc4ff> .

