        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Description: silk satin brocaded with silk and metal thread,\nDark blue ground with a pattern of confronting birds above a circular arrangement of three flowers on a stem with a pair of leaves at the bottom.  In between this arrangement is a small floral sprig and above the arrangement is a small flame-like tree. The birds were woven with either light blue or green [visible now only from the back] details.  The predominate colours are pink and white.  The metal thread is silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk.\n\nSee also T.210-1910 for the same design on a smaller scale."@en , "1800s, Persian; Birds"@en ;
